---
/**
 * K Culture Wire — 동남아 도달 분포. (/reach)
 *
 * ── 왜 이 지면인가 ─────────────────────────────────────────────
 * `/titles` 는 같은 448편을 **오래 남은 순 목록**으로만 보여 준다.
 * 「몇 개국에 들어갔나」의 **분포**는 어디에도 없었다. 그런데 그 분포가 이 자료의 핵심이다 —
 * 곡선이 아니라 두 무더기다(6개국 43.3% · 1개국 29.9%, 가운데 넷을 다 합쳐 26.8%).
 *
 * ── 기사와 서로 검산한다 ───────────────────────────────────────
 * `/article/korean-titles-southeast-asia-all-or-nothing` 이 같은 자료로 먼저 나갔다.
 * 이 지면의 숫자가 그 기사와 어긋나면 둘 중 하나가 틀린 것이다. 빌드 뒤 기계로 대조한다.
 *
 * ── ⚠ 차트 진입이지 시청량이 아니다 ───────────────────────────
 * 넷플릭스는 나라마다 10위까지만 낸다. 국가별 목록에는 **시청시간이 없다.**
 * 「얼마나 봤나」로 읽히지 않게 지면에 박는다.
 *
 * ⛔ 광고 자리를 만들지 않았다. Riot Production 승인 전이다.
 */
import WikiTip from '../../layouts/WikiTip.astro';
import data from '../../data/wikitip-reach.json';

const TITLE = 'How far Korean titles travel in Southeast Asia';
const DESC =
  'All 448 Korean titles that reached a Netflix Top 10 in six Southeast Asian markets since 2021, '
  + 'sorted by how many of the six they reached. 43.3% reached all six; 29.9% reached exactly one.';

const 여섯 = data.buckets.find((b) => b.countries === 6)!;
const 하나 = data.buckets.find((b) => b.countries === 1)!;
const 가운데 = data.buckets.filter((b) => b.countries > 1 && b.countries < 6);
const 가운데합 = +가운데.reduce((s, b) => s + b.share, 0).toFixed(1);
const 최대 = Math.max(...data.buckets.map((b) => b.n));
const 합계 = data.buckets.reduce((s, b) => s + b.n, 0);

const jsonLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Dataset',
  name: TITLE,
  description: DESC,
  temporalCoverage: `${data.weekFrom}/${data.weekTo}`,
  creator: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'K Culture Wire' },
  isBasedOn: ['https://www.netflix.com/tudum/top10'],
};
---

<WikiTip title={TITLE} description={DESC} jsonLd={jsonLd} canonical="https://www.kculturewire.com/reach">
  <h1>How far Korean titles travel in Southeast Asia</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    {data.titleCount} Korean titles have reached a Netflix Top 10 in {data.region} across
    {' '}{data.weekCount} weeks, {data.weekFrom} to {data.weekTo}. Sorted by how many of the six
    markets each one reached, they do not form a curve.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>Two piles, and very little in between</h2>
    <ul class="dist">
      {data.buckets.map((b) => (
        <li>
          <span class="k">{b.countries} {b.countries === 1 ? 'country' : 'countries'}</span>
          <span class="bar" style={`--w:${(b.n / 최대) * 100}%`}></span>
          <span class="v"><b>{b.n}</b> · {b.share}%</span>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ul>
    <p class="note">
      <b>{여섯.share}%</b> reached all six and <b>{하나.share}%</b> reached exactly one. The four
      middle rows hold <b>{가운데합}%</b> between them. A Korean title released into this region
      mostly behaves as a regional release or a single-market event, and rarely as anything else.
      {' '}<a href="/article/korean-titles-southeast-asia-all-or-nothing">The full story →</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What each pile is made of</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Reached</th><th>Titles</th><th>Share</th><th>Avg weeks</th><th>Series / films</th><th>Hit #1 somewhere</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {data.buckets.map((b) => (
            <tr class={b.countries === 6 || b.countries === 1 ? 'edge' : ''}>
              <td class="nm">{b.countries} of {data.countries}</td>
              <td class="tot">{b.n}</td><td>{b.share}%</td>
              <td>{b.avgWeeks}</td><td>{b.tv} / {b.film}</td><td>{b.peak1}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      The titles that reach all six also last longest once there — {여섯.avgWeeks} weeks on average
      against {하나.avgWeeks} for the single-market titles. Whatever carries a title across the region
      also keeps it on the chart when it arrives.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Series travel. Films mostly do not.</h2>
    <div class="scroll-x">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Format</th><th>Titles</th><th>Avg countries</th><th>Avg weeks</th><th>Reached all six</th><th>Hit #1 somewhere</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {data.formats.map((f) => (
            <tr>
              <td class="nm">{f.type}</td>
              <td>{f.n}</td><td class="tot">{f.avgCountries}</td>
              <td>{f.avgWeeks}</td><td>{f.all6}</td><td>{f.peak1}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="note">
      <b>Part of the weeks column is mechanical and we are not hiding it.</b> A film is one sitting
      and a series is sixteen episodes, so a series holds a chart slot longer almost by construction.
      The countries column is not a runtime artefact — reaching Indonesia and not Thailand is a
      separate event from staying on a chart for six weeks — and on that measure the gap is nearly
      two markets.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="src">
    <h2>Where these numbers come from</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Netflix</b> — {data.source}</li>
      <li>
        <b>The buckets add up.</b> {data.buckets.map((b) => b.n).join(' + ')} = {합계}, the full set
        of Korean titles that charted anywhere in the six markets.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Chart entry, not viewing.</b> Netflix publishes ten rows per country per week and no hours
        figure for country lists. A title watched steadily without breaking into a top ten is absent
        here, and nothing on this page says how much anything was watched.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Not simultaneous.</b> Country count is how many of the six a title charted in at any point
        across the {data.weekCount} weeks. A title that hit Vietnam in 2022 and Thailand in 2024 counts as two.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Six markets, not all of Southeast Asia.</b> Netflix publishes lists for {data.region}.
        Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar and Brunei are not in this data and nothing here describes them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>{data.peak1} of {data.titleCount}</b> reached number one in at least one of the six at least once.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <p class="back"><a href="/">&larr; Back to the front page</a></p>
</WikiTip>

<style>
  h1 { margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: 1.7rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--muted); }
  section { margin: 0 0 2.5rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin: 0 0 .7rem; letter-spacing: -.01em; }
  .note { font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted); margin: .9rem 0 0; line-height: 1.6; }

  /* 두 무더기가 눈에 보여야 한다 — 막대 길이로 U자를 드러낸다 */
  .dist { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .dist li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 5.5rem 1fr 5.5rem; align-items: center;
             gap: .6rem; padding: .3rem 0; }
  .k { font-size: .8rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .bar { height: 1.05rem; border-radius: 3px; background: var(--accent); width: var(--w);
         min-width: 2px; opacity: .85; }
  .v { font-size: .8rem; color: var(--muted); text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .v b { color: var(--ink); font-size: .92rem; }

  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: .85rem; }
  th, td { padding: .45rem .55rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); text-align: right;
           white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  th { font-size: .72rem; letter-spacing: .03em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted);
       font-weight: 700; }
  th:first-child, td.nm { text-align: left; }
  td.tot { font-weight: 700; }
  tr.edge td { background: var(--card); }

  .src ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.7; }
  .src li { margin: .45rem 0; }
  .src b { color: var(--ink); }
  .back { margin-top: 2.5rem; font-size: .9rem; }
</style>
